# KlassApp — Frontend Conventions

## Tooling (Phase 3.5 — Vite sole bundler, Jul 2026)

- **Vite 8** + `laravel-vite-plugin` — sole bundler. Scripts: `npm run dev` (= Vite HMR) / `npm run build` (= production). There is **no** Laravel Mix / `webpack.mix.js` / `npm run production`.
- **Vue 3.5.40** via **`@vue/compat` MODE 2** — Options API, `Vue.component()` registration. Browser `Vue.version` must start with `3`. Alias `vue` → `@vue/compat` in `vite.config.js`; runtime `configureCompat({ MODE: 2, … })` via `resources/assets/js/vue-compat.js`.
- **ESM only (Phase 3.1)**: `resources/assets/js/app.js` + `bootstrap.js` use `import`/`export`. Do **not** reintroduce `require()` — Vite-served `npm run dev` runs native ESM (`require is not defined`). Prefer new shared modules (`vue-compat.js`, `event-bus.js`, `jquery-global.js`) over circular imports from `app.js`.
- **Install**: `npm install` (`.npmrc` has `legacy-peer-deps=true`). **Scoped debt**: several Vue-2-era packages still declare `peerDependencies.vue` that reject Vue 3 — see knowledge.md Phase 3.5 closeout. Do not remove the flag without replacing those packages.
- **Tailwind v4.3.3** — CSS-first `@theme` in `resources/css/tailwind.css` (no `tailwind.config.js`). Vite plugin: `@tailwindcss/vite`. Sass entry `resources/assets/sass/app.scss` is plain CSS post–Phase 2b (`@apply` not reintroduced in SCSS).
- **Pusher / Echo**: `import.meta.env.VITE_PUSHER_APP_KEY` / `VITE_PUSHER_APP_CLUSTER` only (Mix dual-read removed in 3.5). Empty key → skip `new Echo(...)`.
- **Blade**: layouts use `@vite([...])` for JS/CSS entries — not `mix()` / not bare `asset('js/app.js')` for the app bundle. Production must **not** leave `public/hot` (dev server pointer).
- **Playwright** available in `node_modules` for E2E testing.

## Soft SFC compiler diagnostics

Mix’s `VueCompatSoftCompilerErrorsPlugin` is gone with Mix. Soft SFCs that previously only warned under Mix were cleaned on `main` (~42) so Vite’s strict SFC compiler can build. New template compiler errors hard-fail `npm run build` / `npm run dev` — fix the SFC; do not reintroduce a Mix softener.

## ds-* Pattern Library

The project uses a `ds-*` CSS class convention for dashboard components:

| Pattern | Purpose | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `ds-kpi-card` | KPI metric card (icon + value + label) | Student count, teacher count, fee totals |
| `ds-kpi-icon-wrap` | Icon container inside KPI card | Colored icon background |
| `ds-kpi-value` | Metric number text | Bold large font |
| `ds-kpi-label` | Metric description label | Muted small text |
| `ds-page-head` | Page header wrapper | Flex row with title + action button |
| `ds-page-head-title` | Page heading | `<h1>` styled |
| `ds-btn` | Base button | Shared button base styles |
| `ds-btn-primary` | Primary action button | Colored variant |
| `ds-btn-sm` | Small button size | Compact variant |

These are defined in `resources/assets/sass/` (custom SCSS). The original `@apply` directives that derived some of their values from Tailwind were replaced with hardcoded CSS in Phase 2b — changing Tailwind utility values will **not** automatically propagate to these selectors anymore. Stick to existing patterns rather than introducing new utility classes.

## Mobile-First Responsive Standards

- **Breakpoints tested**: 375px (small mobile), 414px (large mobile), 768px (tablet), 1280px+ (desktop)
- **Layout approach**: Stacked cards on mobile, multi-column on desktop — never horizontal scroll
- **Verification**: Confirm with real screenshots at each breakpoint, not computed CSS values
- **The project has had regressions from assuming CSS values match rendered output** — always render and capture visually

## Sidebar Convention (Option 3)

- Sidebar uses the established "Option 3" icon set
- Group hover-preview pattern on desktop (expands on hover over group indicator)
- Consistent with Pulse dashboard standard

## Layout Tailwind Source Matrix

Not all layouts load the same Tailwind source — **check which layout a page renders through before assuming a utility will work**:

| Layout | Tailwind source |
|---|---|
| `layouts/app.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 via `@vite` |
| `layouts/superadmin-app.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 via `@vite` |
| `layouts/empty.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 via `@vite` |
| `layouts/main.blade.php` | Local `tailwind.css` v4 via `@vite` |
| `layouts/minimal.blade.php` | `app.css` only — **no** dedicated `tailwind.css` link |
| `layouts/admission.blade.php` | CDN v1.1.3 + `app.css` — **no** local v4 Tailwind link |
| `layouts/video.blade.php` | CDN v1.1.3 + `app.css` — **no** local v4 Tailwind link |

Landing pages (`landing.blade.php`, `landing2.blade.php`) use Tailwind Play CDN (`cdn.tailwindcss.com`) — self-configured.

### @Apply → Hardcoded CSS

The `@apply` rules in `adminstyle.scss` / `style.scss` were replaced with hardcoded CSS in Phase 2b (sass-loader / Vite Sass cannot resolve Tailwind’s CSS-first entry). Selectors like `.admin-h1`, `.tw-form-control`, `.submit-btn` are plain CSS. Prefer raw CSS values when editing them, or `@apply` only inside `resources/css/tailwind.css`.

### Regression Risk: Silent Property Drops

SCSS strips `//` comments on compile. If investigating missing CSS, grep `// UNKNOWN:` under `resources/assets/sass/` — not compiled CSS artifacts.

### v4 Preflight: Border Color Change

Tailwind v4 default `border-color` is `currentColor`. Bare `border` / `border-{side}` need an explicit color utility (e.g. `border-gray-200`). `.dashboard-kpi-card` is already protected in `dashboard-refresh.css`.
